WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.960
Cut every nerve to a loop of a dog's gut, then drip weak acid onto its lining.

2
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.140
The pancreas still secretes its juice.

3
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.940
It sits in a different part of the abdomen, and the leading view said the gut

4
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.240
instructs it by nerve.

5
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.300
But no wire joins the two organs now.

6
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.160
What carried the message?

7
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:28.903
The answer was a chemical, later named secretin.

8
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:34.063
Acid released it from the gut lining, and the blood carried it to the pancreas.

9
00:00:34.663 --> 00:00:39.923
An extract of the lining, filtered and injected into a vein, made the pancreas

10
00:00:39.923 --> 00:00:41.303
secrete even more.

11
00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:45.003
But molecules can also drift on their own.

12
00:00:45.423 --> 00:00:47.483
So why ride the blood at all?

13
00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:50.937
That drift is called diffusion.

14
00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:54.797
A diffusing molecule is not heading anywhere.

15
00:00:55.077 --> 00:01:01.217
It wanders. The typical time to wander a distance grows with the square of that

16
00:01:01.217 --> 00:01:07.717
distance. So diffusion punishes distance: a far target waits much longer than a near

17
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:08.717
one.

18
00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:13.490
Take a small molecule in water, and change only the distance.

19
00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:20.410
It crosses a synaptic gap, 20 nanometers wide, in a fraction of a microsecond.

20
00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.430
It crosses a millimeter in about 8 minutes.

21
00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:28.690
It crosses a centimeter in about 14 hours.

22
00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:34.970
The centimeter is only ten times farther than the millimeter, yet it costs hours

23
00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.010
instead of minutes.

24
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:42.490
Past a millimeter or so, diffusion cannot deliver a message that must act within a

25
00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:48.090
minute. So a gland releases its hormone into the blood, which circulates around the

26
00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.450
body in about a minute.

27
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.690
Fast local signals do the opposite.

28
00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:58.750
A nerve cell releases its message into a gap only tens of nanometers wide.

29
00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:04.250
The message arrives almost at once, and almost none of it reaches anyone else.

30
00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:11.103
The extract reached every organ in the dog, yet only the pancreas answered.

31
00:02:11.803 --> 00:02:14.243
A signal does not choose its audience.

32
00:02:14.823 --> 00:02:15.963
The receiver does.

33
00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:23.223
Epinephrine, a hormone, makes liver cells break down glycogen, fat cells break down

34
00:02:23.223 --> 00:02:25.543
fat, and the heart beat harder.

35
00:02:26.423 --> 00:02:33.023
So keep this rule: far messages ride the blood, and the receptor decides who answers.
